--TEST--
hovering an attribute's name shows its declaration with its sites and keys, the `///` doc above it, and the owner whose descendants may use it, `rule:attributes/an-attribute-is-declared-with-its-sites`
--FILE--
<?nvs
abstract class Storable
{
    /// Adds a database index over one or more columns of this table.
    repeatable attribute Index on class {
        /// The column names, separated by commas.
        columns: string,
        unique?: bool,
    }
}

#[In<|>dex(columns: "email")]
class Order extends Storable {}
--REQUEST--
hover
--EXPECT--
```nvs
repeatable attribute Storable::Index on class {
    columns: string,
    unique?: bool,
}
```

Adds a database index over one or more columns of this table.

Declared in `Storable`. You can use it only on classes that extend or implement `Storable`, and on their members.
